INFO  2026-08-15T01:40:02 +0ms service=session.summary body=I now have the full picture of the diff. A note on process first: the Bash tool is completely broken in this session (every command — even `pwd`, sandboxed or not — dies in the bwrap wrapper with `bwrap: Can't mkdir /mnt/c/Users/WsiAccount/.claude: Permission denied`, for subagents too), so I could not run `git diff`. I reconstructed the review scope from git metadata via the Read tool instead:

- `origin/crb-base-mfc-fscompat` does not exist; the base ref exists only as the **local** branch `crb-base-mfc-fscompat` → `d86d2dc`, which is exactly `HEAD~2` of the detached HEAD (`b64c1ca`).
- The diff therefore consists of two commits: `2136fd6` "feat: redirect cache + analytics writes to /tmp on Vercel" and `b64c1ca` "refactor: extract dataDir() helper for server-side persistence".
- Files changed: `app/lib/utils/dataDir.ts` (new), `app/lib/llm/cache.ts` (cache dir now `dataDir("cache")`), `app/lib/analytics/persist.ts` (data dir now `dataDir()`, plus a new comment). I read all of them in full, plus their consumers (`callLlm.ts`, `app/api/analytics/route.ts`), the README, and `.gitignore`.

The change itself is sound: `dataDir()` picks `/tmp` when `process.env.VERCEL` is set (the only writable path on Vercel Functions) and `<cwd>/data` otherwise; both write sites go through it; all cache/analytics writes in `callLlm.ts` are already wrapped in try/catch so failures stay non-fatal; no user input reaches any path construction. I found no correctness or security bugs — only documentation and hygiene issues.


**[P2] app/lib/analytics/persist.ts:6 - Comment references a "Deploy to Vercel" README section that doesn't exist in this branch**

The new comment says "see Deploy to Vercel in README," but this branch's README.md has no such section (it exists only in the upstream repo's newer README). The diff changes Vercel deployment behavior without any README documentation, and the comment sends readers to a section they can't find — per this repo's documentation-maintenance guidelines, the README section should be added (or the reference dropped) in the same change.

**[P3] app/lib/utils/dataDir.ts:12 - New helper has no unit test**

The repo convention (CLAUDE.md: "Write tests alongside implementation") isn't followed for this new helper, whose env-var branching and subpath joining are trivially testable; a test would also have caught that the `VERCEL` branch is only exercised in production.

**[P3] app/lib/utils/dataDir.ts:13 - Writes land in the shared /tmp root instead of an app-namespaced subdirectory**

On Vercel, `analytics.jsonl` and the `cache/` directory are created directly under `/tmp`, which is shared with anything else in the runtime (other libraries commonly create `/tmp/cache` or temp files there). Using a namespaced base like `/tmp/mfc-data` would avoid mingling app persistence with unrelated temp files and make `clearAnalyticsEntries`/cache reads immune to foreign files. body
